# wave with three-cell pulse edges instead of one, so the centred flux
# radiates no wake worth the name and the halo stays at its loaded value
# to a part in 1e3.  That is what makes a BITWISE comparison possible at
# a positive offset: on the sharp deck the null twin drives cells down
# onto the positivity floor, and no positive offset can be inert against
# a cell below it (the input guard requires rho_off to exceed that
# floor, so the two bands necessarily overlap).
